.TH "PB-TEAM-SSO-SETUP" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-sso-setup - Open the WorkOS Admin Portal to verify a domain and connect your identity provider


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team sso setup <team> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print, and open in a browser where possible, a short-lived WorkOS Admin Portal link for one setup step. Use --step domain to verify a domain with a DNS TXT record, then --step sso to connect the identity provider with the guide for your provider. The team needs enough seats; the first run creates its WorkOS organization.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for setup

.PP
\fB--step\fP="sso"
	domain (verify a domain) or sso (connect the identity provider)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team-sso(1)\fP
